==Strategy==
The key to this straightforward stage is to safely dispose of the Capies with whatever units you have at your disposal, then finish off Jones and destroy the enemy base. You'll have around two minutes and forty seconds. Since Jones spawns at the start, you should lure the Capies and try to finish them outside of his range, rather than knocking them back. The Sir Seals serve to provide a little more extra money.

For a video on learning how to sync and align the Capies, see the second video in the walkthrough section.

Send out three or more cheap meatshields and some powerful anti-red attackers against Capy. Some possible options include [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier]], [[Swordsman Cat (Rare Cat)|Elemental Duelist]] and [[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cutter]]. CC units like [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] and general attackers like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can]] also work wonders, as when used properly, Capy has a hard time hitting them, even in swarms. Ideally, Awakened Bahamut is saved for defeating Jones alongside Ramen. Ubers that can overpower reds and angels are also welcome here, as you need all the damage you can get.

